.\" waggle(1) - manual page, mdoc(7) macros.
.\" Render:  mandoc -a man/waggle.1     Lint:  mandoc -T lint man/waggle.1
.Dd June 6, 2026
.Dt WAGGLE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm waggle
.Nd zero-dependency Node-to-Hive blockchain client
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Nm
.Cm help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the Hive blockchain and acts on it from the shell: it builds, signs,
and broadcasts transactions \(em votes, posts, comments, follows, reblogs,
transfers, and reward claims \(em using only Node built-ins, with no npm
dependency tree.
Reads need no keys.
Writes need the relevant Hive private key, supplied through the environment
.Pq see Sx ENVIRONMENT ;
.Nm
never writes keys to disk.
.Pp
The first argument is a
.Ar command .
With no command, or with
.Cm help ,
.Fl h ,
or
.Fl Fl help ,
.Nm
prints a usage summary.
Results are printed to standard output as pretty-printed JSON, or as a bare
string for scalar results.
.Ss Read commands
These query a Hive node and require no keys.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm globals
Print the dynamic global properties of the chain.
.It Cm refblock
Print the transaction-as-proof-of-stake reference data:
.Va ref_block_num ,
.Va ref_block_prefix ,
and the chain head time.
.It Cm account Ar name
Print the account object for
.Ar name .
.It Cm content Ar author Ar permlink
Print a post or comment via
.Li condenser_api.get_content .
.It Cm post Ar author Ar permlink
Print a post via the bridge API
.Li bridge.get_post .
.It Cm ranked Ar sort Op Ar tag Op Ar limit
Print ranked posts.
.Ar sort
is one of
.Cm trending , hot , created ,
and the other bridge sorts.
.It Cm posts Ar account Op Ar sort Op Ar limit
Print an account's posts.
.Ar sort
is one of
.Cm blog , feed , posts , replies .
.It Cm profile Ar account
Print an account's social profile.
.It Cm followers Ar account Op Ar limit
Print the accounts following
.Ar account .
.It Cm following Ar account Op Ar limit
Print the accounts
.Ar account
follows.
.It Cm follow-count Ar account
Print follower and following counts for
.Ar account .
.It Cm history Ar account Op Ar limit
Print the account's operation history.
.El
.Ss Write commands
These build, sign, and broadcast a transaction, and need the relevant private
key in the environment.
Social actions use the
.Ev WAGGLE_POSTING_KEY ;
value transfers use the
.Ev WAGGLE_ACTIVE_KEY .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm vote Ar author Ar permlink Op Ar weight
Vote on a post.
.Ar weight
is in basis points and defaults to
.Li 10000
.Pq 100% .
Needs the posting key.
.It Cm unvote Ar author Ar permlink
Remove a vote
.Pq weight 0 .
Needs the posting key.
.It Cm publish Ar title Ar body Op Ar tag
Publish a new top-level post.
If
.Ar body
is
.Sq Fl
the body is read from standard input.
Needs the posting key.
.It Cm reply Ar parentAuthor Ar parentPermlink Ar body
Reply to a post or comment.
If
.Ar body
is
.Sq Fl
the body is read from standard input.
Needs the posting key.
.It Cm transfer Ar to Ar amount Op Ar memo
Transfer value, e.g.\&
.Li "1.000 HIVE" .
Needs the active key.
The memo is sent as plaintext.
.It Cm follow Ar account
Follow
.Ar account .
Needs the posting key.
.It Cm unfollow Ar account
Unfollow
.Ar account .
Needs the posting key.
.It Cm reblog Ar author Ar permlink
Reblog a post to your blog.
Needs the posting key.
.It Cm claim
Claim all pending rewards for the configured account.
Needs the posting key.
.El
.Ss Utility commands
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm pubkey Ar wif
Derive and print the
.Li STM
public key for a WIF private key, entirely offline.
.It Cm whoami
Print the configured account and the public keys derived from the configured
private keys.
.It Cm help
Print the usage summary.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width WAGGLE_POSTING_KEY
.It Ev WAGGLE_ACCOUNT
Default account for write commands, and the observer for reads that accept one.
.It Ev WAGGLE_POSTING_KEY
WIF posting key, used by
.Cm vote , publish , reply , follow , reblog ,
and
.Cm claim .
.It Ev WAGGLE_ACTIVE_KEY
WIF active key, used by
.Cm transfer .
.It Ev WAGGLE_OWNER_KEY
WIF owner key.
.It Ev WAGGLE_MEMO_KEY
WIF memo key.
.It Ev WAGGLE_NODES
Comma-separated list of node base URLs to use instead of the built-in
defaults.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A non-zero exit means the command was unknown or the operation failed.
The error message is printed to standard error, prefixed with
.Ql waggle: .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Read an account, no keys required:
.Pp
.Dl $ waggle account hiveio
.Pp
Print the five trending posts in the
.Li hive
tag:
.Pp
.Dl $ waggle ranked trending hive 5
.Pp
Derive a public key from a WIF, offline:
.Pp
.Dl $ waggle pubkey 5J...
.Pp
Vote at 50% after exporting a posting key:
.Pp
.Dl $ export WAGGLE_ACCOUNT=alice WAGGLE_POSTING_KEY=5J...
.Dl $ waggle vote bob a-post 5000
.Pp
Publish a post whose body is piped in from a file:
.Pp
.Dl $ waggle publish \(dqHello Hive\(dq - hive < post.md
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa scripts/waggle.mjs
The command-line entry point.
.It Pa lib/client.mjs
The library entry point, exporting the
.Vt Waggle
class.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr node 1
.Pp
The library API and the byte-level derivations are documented under the
package's
.Pa docs/
directory and
.Pa README.md .
.Sh STANDARDS
.Nm
speaks Hive JSON-RPC 2.0 (the condenser positional and bridge named-object
conventions), graphene binary serialization, and secp256k1 with RFC 6979
deterministic
.Ar k
and the graphene canonical-signature rule.
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was written for the 561-group repository as a from-the-ground-up rederivation
of a Hive client, taking only Node built-ins as given.
It is named for the bees' waggle dance, by which a hive shares where to go.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An emsenn Aq Mt emsenn@emsenn.net .
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
is experimental.
Transfers carry plaintext memos; encrypted memos are not implemented.
Only single-signature authorities are assembled, and the chain id and
.Li STM
address prefix are pinned to Hive mainnet.
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Private keys are read only from the environment and are never written to disk
by
.Nm .
A WIF on the command line
.Pq for example to Cm pubkey
may be recorded in your shell history; prefer the environment for secrets.
